# ============================================
# Bulky / generated artifacts (keep out of git)
# ============================================

# DataPipeline data_cache - large untracked source assets (folder itself mirrors
# ModelPipeline's data_cache pattern). Superseded OD_MS_DataBackups_Bulk/ (removed 2026-07-26).
DataPipeline/data_cache/full_corpus/
DataPipeline/data_cache/samples/sec_finrag_1M_sample.parquet
DataPipeline/data_cache/samples/sec_finrag_1M_sample_filtered.parquet
DataPipeline/data_cache/reference/

# Graphify: everything generated is ignored, only the human-readable report is
# tracked. Deny-then-allow rather than listing artifacts, because the old
# path-anchored patterns missed anything nested: `graphify .` writes a dated
# subdirectory (graphify-out/2026-07-30/) whose graph.json is 2.1MB, and
# cost.json / manifest.json / .graphify_* had no rule at all.
graphify-out/**
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md

# macOS filesystem noise
.DS_Store

# Revival scratch workspace (throwaway inspection/upload scripts)
ModelPipeline/revival_scratch/

# src_edgar_incremental scratch/test-run outputs (manifests, intermediate
# parquets from experimental runs) - pipeline code is tracked, outputs are not
DataPipeline/src_edgar_incremental/manifests/

# DataPipeline's own copy of the production fact table + the incremental
# batches that fed it - regenerate via src_edgar_incremental/, don't hand-edit
# (see data_cache/README.md). Backups live in S3, not git, for these.
DataPipeline/data_cache/stage1_facts/
DataPipeline/data_cache/incremental_batches/

# Same reasoning, for the KPI/numeric fact table - regenerate via
# src_metrics/run_pipeline.py, S3 is the source of truth.
DataPipeline/data_cache/metrics_fact/
# Bulk data purged from git history 2026-07-29 (see GIT_HISTORY_CLEANUP_PLAN.md).
# All of this is regenerable or backed up to S3 / the Seagate archive at
# FinSights_Backup_20260729/. The .gitkeep files stay tracked to preserve layout.
ModelPipeline/finrag_ml_tg1/data_cache/stage1_facts/
ModelPipeline/finrag_ml_tg1/data_cache/analysis_exports/
ModelPipeline/finrag_ml_tg1/data_cache/qa_manual_exports/
DataPipeline/data_cache/samples/
DataPipeline/src_aws_etl/data_exports_testing/

# ============================================
# Audit 2026-07-29: any data cache / table / JSON output is ignored regardless of
# size (policy: volume/size never justifies tracking a regenerable data file).
# Dimension/reference lookup tables - small (3-25KB) but still data_cache OUTPUT,
# not source. Source of truth: DATA_MERGE_ASSETS/DIMENSION_TABLES/ in S3
# (previously kept tracked deliberately; that decision is superseded).
# ============================================
DataPipeline/data_cache/dimensions/
ModelPipeline/finrag_ml_tg1/data_cache/dimensions/

# KPI fact table cache - ModelPipeline's copies (DataPipeline's own copy already
# ignored above via data_cache/metrics_fact/). Regenerate via
# platform_core/data_preparation.py or pull from S3.
ModelPipeline/finrag_ml_tg1/data_cache/metrics_fact/
ModelPipeline/finrag_ml_tg1/rag_modules_src/metric_pipeline/data/

# Scratch/trial data - throwaway by name and by convention.
ModelPipeline/finrag_ml_tg1/data_cache/trial_data_incr/

# MLflow run-tracking store for the production pipeline (synthesis_pipeline/
# mlflow_tracker.py) - regenerated on every run, never meant to be committed.
# Separate from MLFlow_POC/, which has its own nested .gitignore.
ModelPipeline/mlruns/

# src_metrics_legacy - superseded pipeline (see DataPipeline/CLAUDE.md); the code
# stays as reference, its output tables don't.
DataPipeline/src_metrics_legacy/*.parquet
DataPipeline/src_metrics_legacy/metrics_output/

# One-off manual data exports from ad hoc research (csv/xlsx dumps) - the SQL
# scripts and notebooks in the rest of data_engineering_research/ stay tracked
# as genuine research reference; only the raw table exports are cache-shaped.
DataPipeline/data_engineering_research/duckdb_data_engineering/manual_export_analysis/*.csv
DataPipeline/data_engineering_research/duckdb_data_engineering/manual_export_analysis/*.xlsx

# Microsoft Office lock/temp files (e.g. ~$Finance_RAG_HLD_v1.xlsx) - created
# automatically while a file is open, accidental to commit, never source.
~$*
